1
00:00:06,473 --> 00:00:09,340
- Are the men ready to cause chaos in Clun?
- Yes, my lord.

2
00:00:09,409 --> 00:00:11,536
This scheme sounds elaborate.

3
00:00:11,611 --> 00:00:16,480
Stop whining, Gisborne. If I'd wanted a
wife, I would have found one with better legs.

4
00:00:16,549 --> 00:00:18,983
Trust me, Carter's a godsend.

5
00:00:19,085 --> 00:00:20,746
Shoulders back.

6
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:24,187
- He kills people for fun.
- Well, then, why are we paying him?

7
00:00:25,325 --> 00:00:26,952
Fun...

8
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:28,494
and money.

9
00:00:46,679 --> 00:00:48,044
Look at the hands.

10
00:00:57,424 --> 00:01:00,484
Ah. Morning, Carter. This is, er, Gisborne.

11
00:01:03,763 --> 00:01:05,993
My Lord Sheriff.

12
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:10,362
Respect, Gisborne, hm? I like it.

13
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:14,006
Why don't you ever kiss my ring, hm?

14
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:16,599
So... you know what you're going to do?

15
00:01:16,676 --> 00:01:20,544
Retrieve the Great Pact of Nottingham
and kill Robin Hood.

16
00:01:20,613 --> 00:01:23,946
Believe me, my lord,
nothing would give me greater pleasure.

17
00:01:24,017 --> 00:01:26,451
Robin Hood is as good as dead.

18
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:20,299
Robin. Sheriff's men.

19
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:24,936
Wait. You don't want them
to see you with outlaws.

20
00:02:25,011 --> 00:02:28,344
I don't care, they're attacking the village.
Let's get them.

21
00:02:28,414 --> 00:02:32,475
- Why are they doing this?
- Why? Robin, there isn't time for why.

22
00:02:32,552 --> 00:02:34,520
- Let's go.
- Marian. The way to...

23
00:02:34,587 --> 00:02:36,452
- Come on!
- Marian!

24
00:02:39,025 --> 00:02:40,925
- There's too many of them.
- Much.

25
00:02:54,741 --> 00:02:56,333
- Marian!
- Ah!

26
00:03:05,218 --> 00:03:07,379
You... stay there.

27
00:03:22,569 --> 00:03:24,264
Who is that?

28
00:03:24,337 --> 00:03:26,134
Robin. Gallows!

29
00:03:36,916 --> 00:03:39,180
Friend, behind you!

30
00:03:57,637 --> 00:04:01,539
- The sheriff's men are running away.
- Oh, my love. Oh.

31
00:04:01,608 --> 00:04:03,599
- Oh, you're saved.
- He's good.

32
00:04:04,944 --> 00:04:06,741
He's very good.

33
00:04:22,562 --> 00:04:25,656
- Don't ever tie me up.
- Well, you didn't listen to your orders.

34
00:04:25,732 --> 00:04:28,200
- People were dying.
- Marian, you can't be seen with us.

35
00:04:28,301 --> 00:04:31,031
Why not? Robin, I am with you.

36
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:33,629
Because if the Sheriff
finds out, or Gisborne,

37
00:04:33,706 --> 00:04:37,073
- then you can never go back to the castle.
- I don't want to go back.

38
00:04:37,143 --> 00:04:40,806
Well, I'm glad. But you're not ready
to make that decision.

39
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:49,482
Thank you, my friend. I owe you my life.

40
00:04:51,424 --> 00:04:53,585
Yes, you do.

41
00:04:53,693 --> 00:04:56,355
But I won't take it just yet. Carter.

42
00:04:56,963 --> 00:04:58,726
Robin Hood.

43
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:00,322
Much.

44
00:05:01,167 --> 00:05:03,135
Nice, er, move.

45
00:05:03,903 --> 00:05:05,962
- Do I know you?
- I...

46
00:05:06,572 --> 00:05:10,872
We've never met. These soldiers...
Why are they attacking innocent people?

47
00:05:10,943 --> 00:05:13,138
- He's wounded.
- It's nothing.

48
00:05:13,212 --> 00:05:14,873
Whoa! Djaq.

49
00:05:16,249 --> 00:05:19,548
Come on. Get up. Let's get him
out of here. Come on.

50
00:05:19,619 --> 00:05:22,349
John! John! Will, get the quiver.

51
00:05:25,758 --> 00:05:28,124
- I'm sure I've met him.
- Much, let it be.

52
00:05:28,194 --> 00:05:30,754
I'm sure. I know that face.

53
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,963
Did you fight in the Holy Land?

54
00:05:35,034 --> 00:05:37,594
Yes, but we didn't meet.

55
00:05:39,038 --> 00:05:41,939
- How can you be sure?
- You I'd have remembered.

56
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:47,912
- Why have you come back?
- Stabbed in the back.

57
00:05:48,514 --> 00:05:50,607
Did you get him, the one who did it?

58
00:05:51,851 --> 00:05:55,981
No, but I've been biding my time, preparing.

59
00:05:56,689 --> 00:06:00,125
Well, you look prepared today.
Could have taken on a whole army of them.

60
00:06:01,394 --> 00:06:04,557
Probably disappointed, though,
with, er, today's wound.

61
00:06:04,630 --> 00:06:08,293
I mean, if you're planning to go back
to the Holy Land and, er, kill him.

62
00:06:09,001 --> 00:06:11,299
- He's here.
- In England?

63
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:16,104
Wasn't me, was it?

64
00:06:17,377 --> 00:06:19,174
It worked, it worked.

65
00:06:19,245 --> 00:06:22,703
Hood saw the poor, innocent people
of Clun being attacked

66
00:06:22,782 --> 00:06:25,717
and then dashed, rather dashingly,
in to save them.

67
00:06:25,785 --> 00:06:29,084
- And we lost several guards.
- Yes. Yes, yes.

68
00:06:29,155 --> 00:06:33,182
It's very unfortunate. Erm... Send
their families a basket of fruit. Small.

69
00:06:34,093 --> 00:06:38,291
But it worked. Carter left with Hood.
Hood could already be dead.

70
00:06:40,133 --> 00:06:43,660
Oh, and by the way, erm...
Marian sent a message.

71
00:06:45,438 --> 00:06:48,134
- What message?
- Hm? Oh. Erm...

72
00:06:48,207 --> 00:06:50,937
"I'm not coming back, get over it

73
00:06:51,010 --> 00:06:53,672
"and, for God's sake,
change your clothes once in a while. "

74
00:06:53,846 --> 00:06:55,814
Very funny.

75
00:06:56,449 --> 00:06:59,475
She ran away. Guy, sit down.

76
00:07:05,358 --> 00:07:07,519
She ran away

77
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:10,084
the minute her dad died. Mm?

78
00:07:11,297 --> 00:07:14,664
Now, what does that tell us? It tells me...

79
00:07:14,734 --> 00:07:19,694
that the crusty one was the only thing
keeping her here.

80
00:07:20,740 --> 00:07:22,571
No.

81
00:07:22,642 --> 00:07:24,610
There was something between us.

82
00:07:25,344 --> 00:07:26,811
No.

83
00:07:26,913 --> 00:07:29,939
She's not coming back, Guy. Move on.

84
00:07:31,984 --> 00:07:34,009
I'll tell you what.

85
00:07:35,054 --> 00:07:38,319
I'll give you a kiss, hm,
if it will make you feel better, huh?

86
00:07:38,391 --> 00:07:41,758
Oh, come along. In fact,
if Hood's dead, I'll give you two kisses.

87
00:07:41,828 --> 00:07:45,286
- Come along. Kissy, give us a kissy.
- Get off me.

88
00:07:49,435 --> 00:07:51,335
Grow up, Gisborne.

89
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:08,079
Are you going to apologize to me?
You could have got me killed.

90
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:11,817
I think you would have got yourself killed
without my help,

91
00:08:11,924 --> 00:08:13,482
charging in like that.

92
00:08:13,559 --> 00:08:17,893
Robin, I've been fighting these idiots
for years. I was the Nightwatchman.

93
00:08:17,964 --> 00:08:20,626
- Remember?
- I know. On your own.

94
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,725
This is a team, Marian.

95
00:08:22,802 --> 00:08:25,270
You went crashing in
and we all had to follow.

96
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:28,273
And in battle that's a cardinal sin.
We work together.

97
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:30,673
You mean they do as you tell them.

98
00:08:30,743 --> 00:08:32,734
Yeah. Yeah, they do.

99
00:08:33,813 --> 00:08:36,805
And, until you learn to do the same,
you can stay here at the camp.

100
00:08:36,916 --> 00:08:39,384
- What?
- I mean it, Marian.

101
00:08:39,452 --> 00:08:41,420
You need to calm down.

102
00:08:43,756 --> 00:08:46,691
I don't need to be mollycoddled, all right?

103
00:08:46,759 --> 00:08:48,750
Good. Because you're not gonna get it here.

104
00:09:09,815 --> 00:09:11,715
Have you been sent to baby-sit me?

105
00:09:16,255 --> 00:09:18,985
Why do you do everything he says?

106
00:09:20,226 --> 00:09:22,751
I thought you used to have
your own men, Little John.

107
00:09:22,828 --> 00:09:25,854
I did. But there can only be one leader.

108
00:09:28,501 --> 00:09:31,402
This is not how I thought it would be,

109
00:09:32,805 --> 00:09:34,670
living in the forest.

110
00:09:36,042 --> 00:09:39,671
I can't breathe... in here.

111
00:09:40,379 --> 00:09:42,574
It's worse than living in the castle.

112
00:09:44,216 --> 00:09:45,945
Come here.

113
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:01,165
It's not the here or there, is it?

114
00:10:02,368 --> 00:10:04,268
It's your father.

115
00:10:04,337 --> 00:10:06,601
You've lost your father.

116
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:12,176
And that's why I want to get on with things.

117
00:10:12,845 --> 00:10:15,507
In time. In time.

118
00:10:37,336 --> 00:10:39,531
You should be resting.

119
00:10:39,605 --> 00:10:42,130
- Things to do.
- What things?

120
00:11:01,427 --> 00:11:03,361
Stay here. Stay here.

121
00:11:03,429 --> 00:11:05,192
I will.

122
00:11:21,213 --> 00:11:22,976
Ah!

123
00:12:33,719 --> 00:12:35,584
Let me guess.

124
00:12:36,322 --> 00:12:39,291
- The Sheriff sent you.
- He wants his Pact back.

125
00:12:40,526 --> 00:12:43,086
- No chance.
- I guaranteed it.

126
00:12:43,162 --> 00:12:45,892
Yeah? Well, you made a mistake.

127
00:12:46,565 --> 00:12:50,023
- Tell me where you've hidden it.
- I'll die first.

128
00:12:50,136 --> 00:12:54,903
No. Your friends will die first,
one by one, till you tell me.

129
00:12:56,175 --> 00:12:58,666
See? That little look back...

130
00:13:00,346 --> 00:13:02,473
you just revealed your weakness.

131
00:13:03,482 --> 00:13:05,245
Never look back, friend.

132
00:13:05,317 --> 00:13:07,148
Now I know I've won.

133
00:13:08,821 --> 00:13:10,789
So...

134
00:13:10,856 --> 00:13:12,756
who shall we start with?

135
00:13:12,825 --> 00:13:14,986
Your little sidekick in the Holy Land?

136
00:13:16,162 --> 00:13:18,323
Or do you have a soft spot for the girl?

137
00:13:19,165 --> 00:13:20,826
I thought so.

138
00:13:33,612 --> 00:13:35,477
Unbelievable!

139
00:13:35,548 --> 00:13:37,175
We took him in.

140
00:13:37,249 --> 00:13:41,276
- We pitied him because he was wounded.
- I think that was his plan, Much.

141
00:13:41,353 --> 00:13:43,378
I know. I knew.

142
00:13:43,455 --> 00:13:45,753
Just... outrageous.

143
00:13:49,728 --> 00:13:52,390
- Marian.
- He'll tell us more

144
00:13:52,464 --> 00:13:54,694
if he knows we're happy to hurt him.

145
00:13:54,767 --> 00:13:57,031
- Won't he?
- That's not how we're doing this.

146
00:13:57,136 --> 00:13:59,127
Speak for yourself.

147
00:14:00,072 --> 00:14:01,972
Just go and cook something.

148
00:14:02,041 --> 00:14:05,135
- What, because I'm a woman?
- No, because I'm hungry!

149
00:14:09,615 --> 00:14:11,378
What are we going to do with him, Robin?

150
00:14:12,785 --> 00:14:14,912
We'll take him back to Nottingham.

151
00:14:14,987 --> 00:14:16,887
He's failed to find the Pact

152
00:14:16,956 --> 00:14:19,015
and he's failed to kill me.

153
00:14:19,124 --> 00:14:22,491
So what do you think the Sheriff will do
to a man who's failed him that badly?

154
00:14:22,561 --> 00:14:24,995
Hang him by the neck.

155
00:14:25,064 --> 00:14:27,032
If he's lucky.

156
00:14:28,434 --> 00:14:30,197
Come on.

157
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:37,304
Wake up.

158
00:14:39,111 --> 00:14:41,477
- What do you want?
- I want Marian.

159
00:14:42,514 --> 00:14:45,381
- You know where she is?
- What do you think?

160
00:14:46,785 --> 00:14:50,221
How am I supposed to find her, then?
She could be anywhere.

161
00:14:50,322 --> 00:14:52,085
Ask around.

162
00:14:53,626 --> 00:14:55,526
Earn your keep.

163
00:14:58,797 --> 00:15:00,389
- Nottingham, then.
- No.

164
00:15:01,533 --> 00:15:03,364
Clun first.

165
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:06,367
Not you, Marian, you're staying here.

166
00:15:06,438 --> 00:15:08,998
- Why?
- Because...

167
00:15:09,074 --> 00:15:12,407
- I think you need some time alone.
- Why?

168
00:15:12,478 --> 00:15:14,469
Because this isn't the
Marian I know and love.

169
00:15:14,546 --> 00:15:16,912
Sorry if you're disappointed
but this is who I am now.

170
00:15:16,982 --> 00:15:19,507
Really? Well, I hope not.

171
00:15:20,452 --> 00:15:22,477
Come on. Let's go.

172
00:15:22,554 --> 00:15:26,513
- Why Clun?
- Because there's something I want him to see.

173
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:28,355
Come on.

174
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:47,811
I'm sorry, Jen. We'll make sure
you and your family eat.

175
00:15:48,981 --> 00:15:51,506
- You have my word.
- Thank you, Robin.

176
00:15:52,318 --> 00:15:54,809
Don't worry, Jen, we'll
set you straight. Here.

177
00:15:59,191 --> 00:16:00,988
Come on.

178
00:16:02,361 --> 00:16:04,329
Her husband died because of you.

179
00:16:05,564 --> 00:16:07,395
I only killed Sheriff's men.

180
00:16:08,267 --> 00:16:11,361
And they only killed villagers
to make you look good.

181
00:16:11,437 --> 00:16:14,600
Now, was that the Sheriff's
idea or was it yours?

182
00:16:14,673 --> 00:16:17,699
- His.
- His. But you were happy to go along with it.

183
00:16:18,677 --> 00:16:22,773
And you were happy to see her husband die
if it meant that you get closer to me.

184
00:16:22,848 --> 00:16:24,577
What's your point, Locksley?

185
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:26,481
My point, assassin...

186
00:16:28,387 --> 00:16:30,548
is there's widows here today,

187
00:16:30,622 --> 00:16:34,718
all trying to comfort children who don't
understand why their father didn't come home,

188
00:16:34,793 --> 00:16:38,320
- and why their mother won't stop crying.
- If you're trying to make me feel sorry,

189
00:16:38,397 --> 00:16:40,957
- you're wasting your time.
- Am I?

190
00:16:41,033 --> 00:16:44,332
Because there's a reason
why you don't like to look back, Carter.

191
00:16:45,304 --> 00:16:47,864
Because you don't want to see
what it is you do.

192
00:16:48,741 --> 00:16:51,141
Because you don't like what you do.

193
00:16:51,210 --> 00:16:52,905
And you know how I know that?

194
00:16:54,413 --> 00:16:56,506
It's because I used to be like you.

195
00:16:58,017 --> 00:17:00,042
I've killed in the Holy Land as well.

196
00:17:00,586 --> 00:17:03,316
- Boo-hoo.
- Boo-hoo.

197
00:17:23,942 --> 00:17:26,934
- You could have had my eye out.
- You've got some nerve,

198
00:17:27,012 --> 00:17:29,105
showing your face in the forest.

199
00:17:29,181 --> 00:17:33,550
I checked you were on your own first. I know
what the lads'll do to me if they get a chance,

200
00:17:33,619 --> 00:17:36,315
- but I figured I owe you this much.
- You're here for me?

201
00:17:36,388 --> 00:17:41,052
Gisborne. Wants me to find you. I mean,
obviously I didn't tell him you'd be here.

202
00:17:41,126 --> 00:17:44,254
- Obviously.
- No, but I'll need to tell him something.

203
00:17:45,164 --> 00:17:49,567
So I was thinking I could tell him you joined
up with the Sisters of the Immaculate Conception.

204
00:17:49,635 --> 00:17:51,899
- Would he believe that?
- Yeah.

205
00:17:51,970 --> 00:17:55,906
Well, I was thinking, you could write a
note, just say you want to be left alone.

206
00:17:55,974 --> 00:17:58,408
Bit of praying, grieving, whatever.

207
00:17:58,510 --> 00:18:00,569
Why would you help me?

208
00:18:00,646 --> 00:18:02,170
Look, I'm not all bad.

209
00:18:02,247 --> 00:18:06,513
Any letters from the convent have
to be sealed by the Mother Superior.

210
00:18:07,453 --> 00:18:09,444
- I can sort that.
- How?

211
00:18:09,521 --> 00:18:11,785
I'm good with nuns.

212
00:18:19,698 --> 00:18:21,461
Sh. You're all right.

213
00:18:21,533 --> 00:18:25,333
I'm not gonna hurt you.
Just want to borrow your ring.

214
00:18:25,404 --> 00:18:27,463
Here we are. Come here.

215
00:18:29,141 --> 00:18:31,473
Lovely. Here we are. Here y'are.

216
00:18:32,377 --> 00:18:35,574
Buy yourself a new habit.
Say a little prayer for me.

217
00:18:40,252 --> 00:18:42,482
All right, Will. Let's go.

218
00:18:44,990 --> 00:18:46,787
Ah!

219
00:18:49,995 --> 00:18:52,088
Are you all right? Everyone!

220
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,961
- Where is he?
- John, we'll check by the road.

221
00:18:57,035 --> 00:18:59,265
You two, down there. Now!

222
00:19:01,206 --> 00:19:04,107
- What about you?
- I'll stay here.

223
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:07,772
Go on. Go. You and me, too.

224
00:20:06,138 --> 00:20:08,368
I accepted a contract to kill you.

225
00:20:09,408 --> 00:20:11,603
I will fulfill that contract.

226
00:20:12,778 --> 00:20:14,973
It's not just a contract.

227
00:20:16,248 --> 00:20:17,909
Is it, Carter?

228
00:20:19,585 --> 00:20:21,917
Much was right, wasn't he?

229
00:20:21,987 --> 00:20:24,080
You did meet in the Holy Land.

230
00:20:24,156 --> 00:20:26,681
He never met me. He met my brother.

231
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:32,091
- What was his name?
- You don't remember? You should.

232
00:20:32,164 --> 00:20:34,132
You killed him.

233
00:20:36,368 --> 00:20:38,836
- What was his name?
- Thomas.

234
00:20:38,904 --> 00:20:40,599
Thomas?

235
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:43,208
Yes. This is for him.

236
00:20:44,309 --> 00:20:46,504
I've waited for this moment.

237
00:20:46,578 --> 00:20:50,742
I've imagined it so many different ways,
meeting you. Killing you.

238
00:20:50,816 --> 00:20:53,751
Good. Well, I hope it
lives up to expectation.

239
00:20:53,819 --> 00:20:55,787
It will. I trained myself.

240
00:20:57,256 --> 00:21:00,191
I'm the best there is and I exist,
Locksley, to kill you.

241
00:21:05,197 --> 00:21:07,165
I didn't kill him, Carter.

242
00:21:08,834 --> 00:21:10,802
You ordered him into a village.

243
00:21:12,037 --> 00:21:14,130
He called for help, but you did not come.

244
00:21:14,706 --> 00:21:16,571
You let him die.

245
00:21:16,642 --> 00:21:18,542
I remember him.

246
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:21,101
- He was a good fighter.
- He was a war hero.

247
00:21:21,179 --> 00:21:23,147
Yeah. And he stopped listening.

248
00:21:24,016 --> 00:21:27,315
He thought he was invincible.
He led the charge into that village.

249
00:21:27,386 --> 00:21:29,616
We told him it was dangerous.
He wouldn't listen.

250
00:21:29,721 --> 00:21:31,313
No.

251
00:21:31,390 --> 00:21:33,153
We tried to save him.

252
00:21:33,225 --> 00:21:34,920
- I tried.
- You're lying.

253
00:21:36,194 --> 00:21:40,460
I was there when they brought back his body.
The stretcher-bearers told me everything.

254
00:21:42,701 --> 00:21:44,532
I told them to make up the story,

255
00:21:45,003 --> 00:21:49,337
so his family would remember him as a war
hero, not as a fool who got himself killed.

256
00:21:51,410 --> 00:21:53,105
Rubbish!

257
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:59,683
He wasn't the only one who died that day.
Morgan Foster died trying to save him.

258
00:21:59,751 --> 00:22:02,117
- Matthew Kent.
- Think I believe this?

259
00:22:02,187 --> 00:22:06,123
You're just afraid to die. You were a coward
then and you're a coward now.

260
00:22:06,191 --> 00:22:08,352
- He cried when he died.
- Liar!

261
00:22:08,427 --> 00:22:12,386
He cried and he said,
"Tell my family I didn't cry.

262
00:22:12,464 --> 00:22:14,125
"Tell them I wasn't crying,

263
00:22:14,199 --> 00:22:17,066
"I was laughing on the
wrong side of my face. "

264
00:22:17,135 --> 00:22:20,764
That's what he used to say,
laughing on the wrong side of your face.

265
00:22:20,839 --> 00:22:22,500
How do you know that?

266
00:22:27,112 --> 00:22:30,570
I know because I held him in my arms
when he died.

267
00:22:31,717 --> 00:22:33,878
No. He was a hero.

268
00:22:34,953 --> 00:22:36,978
You killed him. You're a liar.

269
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:41,083
If you really think I'm
lying, you can kill me.

270
00:22:42,861 --> 00:22:45,523
If you think it'll give you peace...

271
00:22:47,599 --> 00:22:49,499
then kill me now.

272
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:11,086
He was a hero.

273
00:23:12,624 --> 00:23:14,489
Just not on that day.

274
00:23:19,598 --> 00:23:21,429
What am I doing here?

275
00:23:23,668 --> 00:23:25,659
I don't know what I'm doing.

276
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:33,973
Help me.

277
00:23:35,113 --> 00:23:36,876
My brother.

278
00:23:39,351 --> 00:23:41,546
I loved him so much.

279
00:23:53,131 --> 00:23:55,224
It's all right.

280
00:23:55,333 --> 00:23:57,494
Hey.

281
00:23:57,569 --> 00:23:59,298
Come on.

282
00:24:01,606 --> 00:24:03,471
It's all right.

283
00:24:05,177 --> 00:24:06,940
It's all right.

284
00:24:12,050 --> 00:24:13,915
You all right?

285
00:24:17,189 --> 00:24:19,282
Why is he crying?

286
00:24:19,357 --> 00:24:21,291
He's not crying.

287
00:24:23,361 --> 00:24:25,591
He's laughing on the wrong side of his face.

288
00:24:30,035 --> 00:24:32,230
Well, now you know she's safe and well.

289
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:37,865
And how do you know that she's safe and well?

290
00:24:37,943 --> 00:24:40,070
She said.

291
00:24:40,145 --> 00:24:41,737
Did she?

292
00:24:43,715 --> 00:24:45,876
I thought they took a vow of silence.

293
00:24:45,951 --> 00:24:47,748
No, I mean, the, erm...

294
00:24:47,819 --> 00:24:50,913
The Mother Superior said
when she gave me the letter.

295
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:52,684
No.

296
00:24:54,025 --> 00:24:56,960
No. This is not right.

297
00:24:57,028 --> 00:24:58,996
What d'you mean?

298
00:24:59,798 --> 00:25:01,766
Marian cannot take holy orders.

299
00:25:03,134 --> 00:25:04,897
She has a life to lead.

300
00:25:06,638 --> 00:25:09,801
- Saddle my horse.
- Oh, I don't really do saddling.

301
00:25:09,908 --> 00:25:11,773
- Do as you're told.
- Sure.

302
00:25:12,444 --> 00:25:14,537
- Where are we going, then?
- Ripley Convent.

303
00:25:14,613 --> 00:25:18,014
Yeah? Hang on. Doesn't she want to be
on her own? Grieving and...

304
00:25:19,618 --> 00:25:21,779
- Get my horse!
- All right, all right.

305
00:25:24,055 --> 00:25:25,818
Thomas was my hero.

306
00:25:26,825 --> 00:25:28,884
Whatever he did, I had to do, too.

307
00:25:29,594 --> 00:25:33,223
And when he joined the Knights Templar,
I knew I had to follow.

308
00:25:34,666 --> 00:25:36,497
I'd only just joined when...

309
00:25:36,568 --> 00:25:38,365
when he died.

310
00:25:38,436 --> 00:25:40,495
Thomas. You look like him.

311
00:25:41,473 --> 00:25:43,668
That's why I recognized you.

312
00:25:43,742 --> 00:25:46,006
I was determined to carry on for him,

313
00:25:46,111 --> 00:25:47,772
to be as good as him.

314
00:25:47,846 --> 00:25:49,905
To get to the very top.

315
00:25:49,981 --> 00:25:52,472
- I joined the King's private guard.
- Like us.

316
00:25:53,451 --> 00:25:55,476
That's where I heard about you.

317
00:25:55,554 --> 00:25:57,419
Robin this, Robin that,

318
00:25:58,123 --> 00:25:59,954
how great you were.

319
00:26:00,759 --> 00:26:02,818
And it made my blood boil.

320
00:26:04,529 --> 00:26:07,498
And every time I killed,
I imagined I was killing you,

321
00:26:08,333 --> 00:26:10,426
the man who took my brother away from me.

322
00:26:11,002 --> 00:26:14,563
And when I returned,
I came straight to Nottingham,

323
00:26:14,639 --> 00:26:17,836
where the Sheriff has a contract
on your head. £500.

324
00:26:17,943 --> 00:26:19,706
£500?

325
00:26:20,545 --> 00:26:24,072
So I figured his plan to
lure you to the village...

326
00:26:25,016 --> 00:26:27,177
I'd get to you quicker.

327
00:26:27,252 --> 00:26:30,619
So all this death was for personal revenge?

328
00:26:35,927 --> 00:26:38,589
- When did you last see the King?
- Why?

329
00:26:38,663 --> 00:26:40,631
Well, because...

330
00:26:40,732 --> 00:26:42,700
we sent him a message.

331
00:26:43,435 --> 00:26:45,596
A very important message.

332
00:26:45,670 --> 00:26:48,195
The messenger was Roger of Stoke.
Do you know him?

333
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:52,334
I know Roger. No. He was expected
but did not return.

334
00:26:54,379 --> 00:26:56,142
Great.

335
00:26:57,115 --> 00:26:59,606
- So the King knows nothing about Shah Mat?
- Shah-what?

336
00:26:59,718 --> 00:27:01,811
That doesn't concern you.

337
00:27:04,255 --> 00:27:06,689
- What can I do?
- What can you do?

338
00:27:10,161 --> 00:27:12,129
You can do what you set out to do.

339
00:27:12,664 --> 00:27:16,122
Go back to Nottingham,
give the Sheriff back his pact

340
00:27:16,201 --> 00:27:18,692
and one dead outlaw.

341
00:27:22,040 --> 00:27:25,806
I can't believe we're trusting him.
He's tried to kill us.

342
00:27:25,877 --> 00:27:28,437
Of all of us, you and I know
what war can do to a man.

343
00:27:29,447 --> 00:27:32,109
Yeah, I've been to war.
I didn't come back a mad killer.

344
00:27:32,183 --> 00:27:35,380
Well, the demons work
in different ways, don't they?

345
00:27:36,054 --> 00:27:38,818
But they're the same demons.

346
00:27:38,923 --> 00:27:42,086
Yeah, I've got my demons.
You've never held me like you held him.

347
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:43,923
- Much.
- You haven't.

348
00:27:45,597 --> 00:27:49,693
- You've never listened to my story.
- That's because I was there with you.

349
00:27:49,768 --> 00:27:51,599
It's my story, too.

350
00:27:52,203 --> 00:27:54,034
Yeah, I know.

351
00:27:54,673 --> 00:27:56,641
It's just we never talked about it.

352
00:27:57,242 --> 00:27:59,540
- We never talk.
- Well, all right.

353
00:28:01,146 --> 00:28:03,239
- Well, let's talk.
- No.

354
00:28:03,348 --> 00:28:06,010
- Not if you're doing it to humor me, no.
- Come on, Much.

355
00:28:06,117 --> 00:28:08,210
Whatever I say, you never
listen to me, anyway.

356
00:28:08,319 --> 00:28:10,344
You know that's not true.

357
00:28:10,422 --> 00:28:12,890
I told you I recognized
Carter from the Crusades.

358
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:16,953
You didn't believe me.
You'd listen to Marian.

359
00:28:18,463 --> 00:28:20,556
- Spend time with her.
- Much.

360
00:28:21,132 --> 00:28:22,895
Stop.

361
00:28:24,235 --> 00:28:25,998
All right?

362
00:28:30,408 --> 00:28:32,376
Old friend,

363
00:28:32,444 --> 00:28:34,935
you have a special place in my heart.

364
00:28:36,481 --> 00:28:38,244
Do I?

365
00:28:39,851 --> 00:28:41,910
Well, do I really have to say it?

366
00:28:44,055 --> 00:28:45,920
No. Course not.

367
00:28:53,431 --> 00:28:55,422
Just once in a while would be nice.

368
00:28:59,604 --> 00:29:02,937
- What's he doing here?
- Don't worry. It's a long story.

369
00:29:04,976 --> 00:29:06,910
- Allan was here.
- Allan?

370
00:29:06,978 --> 00:29:08,969
Yeah. Gisborne sent him to find me.

371
00:29:09,881 --> 00:29:12,213
- I'll kill him.
- No, he was trying to help.

372
00:29:12,283 --> 00:29:14,808
He sent Gisborne a letter...

373
00:29:14,919 --> 00:29:17,217
saying I'm at Ripley Convent.

374
00:29:17,322 --> 00:29:19,313
The medicine's ready whenever you want.

375
00:29:21,426 --> 00:29:23,360
This could be dangerous, Robin.

376
00:29:24,429 --> 00:29:26,329
What is it you say, John?

377
00:29:26,397 --> 00:29:29,764
- Today's a good day to die?
- What?

378
00:29:29,834 --> 00:29:33,031
We're going to Nottingham
to collect Carter's fee.

379
00:29:33,138 --> 00:29:36,039
- We're gonna give it to the people of Clun.
- We?

380
00:29:36,841 --> 00:29:38,706
I take it that includes me?

381
00:29:38,777 --> 00:29:40,438
I'm sorry, Marian.

382
00:29:40,512 --> 00:29:42,639
Either I'm part of your gang or I'm not.

383
00:29:43,815 --> 00:29:46,841
Marian, for today, please just stay here.

384
00:29:47,986 --> 00:29:49,749
Very well.

385
00:29:50,922 --> 00:29:53,288
- Excuse me?
- I said very well.

386
00:29:53,992 --> 00:29:56,187
I bow to your authority.

387
00:29:56,261 --> 00:29:58,024
Thank you.

388
00:30:00,565 --> 00:30:03,591
- I'm ready.
- We really need him?

389
00:30:03,668 --> 00:30:07,001
Well, the Sheriff's not going to give
the money to anybody else now, is he?

390
00:30:07,071 --> 00:30:09,631
- And if he betrays us?
- Then on my head be it.

391
00:30:09,741 --> 00:30:12,301
- If he does, blame me.
- Good.

392
00:30:12,377 --> 00:30:14,845
- I will. When we're dead.
- Good.

393
00:30:16,748 --> 00:30:18,807
And that's a rule I'd like you to stick to.

394
00:30:19,450 --> 00:30:22,783
- Don't kill anybody unless you have to.
- Spoilsport.

395
00:30:22,854 --> 00:30:24,515
Djaq.

396
00:30:26,124 --> 00:30:28,922
Do your worst. Today is a good day.

397
00:30:30,028 --> 00:30:31,791
I hate sayings.

398
00:30:37,035 --> 00:30:40,004
Creatorum Caeli et terrae;

399
00:30:43,575 --> 00:30:46,567
et in lesum Christum,

400
00:30:49,614 --> 00:30:52,981
Filium Eius, Unicum,

401
00:30:57,021 --> 00:30:58,955
Dominum nostrum,

402
00:31:02,126 --> 00:31:05,425
passus sub Pontio Pilato,

403
00:31:09,434 --> 00:31:10,924
crucifixus...

404
00:31:11,002 --> 00:31:13,732
What are you doing here?
You should be back at camp.

405
00:31:13,805 --> 00:31:16,706
I lied. What are you going to do about it?

406
00:31:17,442 --> 00:31:19,000
Nothing.

407
00:31:47,205 --> 00:31:49,196
Robin.

408
00:32:18,369 --> 00:32:21,930
- What's this?
- Robin Hood, as promised.

409
00:32:24,075 --> 00:32:26,407
- Dead?
- Dead.

410
00:32:27,745 --> 00:32:29,713
Really?

411
00:32:33,418 --> 00:32:35,750
- Did you check him?
- Yes, Sir Guy.

412
00:32:37,588 --> 00:32:40,386
Well, let's make doubly sure, shall we?

413
00:32:42,894 --> 00:32:44,725
Show me his neck.

414
00:32:55,173 --> 00:32:57,368
Guy!

415
00:32:57,442 --> 00:32:59,205
Marian.

416
00:33:01,579 --> 00:33:03,706
What's happening here?

417
00:33:04,015 --> 00:33:06,643
Robin Hood. He's dead.

418
00:33:06,751 --> 00:33:08,582
Congratulations.

419
00:33:09,954 --> 00:33:11,854
I need to speak with you.

420
00:33:13,691 --> 00:33:15,784
In private. Please.

421
00:33:18,963 --> 00:33:20,828
Carry on.

422
00:33:27,739 --> 00:33:31,106
Die Patris omnipotentis,

423
00:33:31,943 --> 00:33:36,175
- sanctam Ecclesiam Catholicam.
- Yes, yes,

424
00:33:36,247 --> 00:33:40,183
that's quite enough of the gobbledegook.
Anywhere on the table will be fine.

425
00:33:52,096 --> 00:33:54,428
Whoo. Exeunt.

426
00:33:55,867 --> 00:33:57,835
Means get out.

427
00:33:58,770 --> 00:34:01,432
- They're with me.
- Not any more.

428
00:34:02,006 --> 00:34:04,531
Wait for me outside. I will pay you then.

429
00:34:17,288 --> 00:34:20,018
We have bad days.

430
00:34:21,859 --> 00:34:23,850
We have good days.

431
00:34:26,230 --> 00:34:29,757
And, when we have...

432
00:34:30,568 --> 00:34:33,594
Robin Hood laid out dead on our table,

433
00:34:33,671 --> 00:34:35,696
we have the best days of our lives!

434
00:34:37,842 --> 00:34:40,003
The, erm, the Great Pact of Nottingham.

435
00:34:42,780 --> 00:34:45,510
D'you know what I'm going
to do with him now?

436
00:34:46,384 --> 00:34:48,352
That's not my concern, my lord.

437
00:34:48,419 --> 00:34:50,546
My work here is done.

438
00:34:50,621 --> 00:34:52,589
Yes.

439
00:34:52,657 --> 00:34:55,387
Is that a subtle hint
that you would like to be paid?

440
00:34:55,460 --> 00:34:57,360
I believe I've fulfilled my contract.

441
00:34:57,428 --> 00:35:00,261
Oh. Yes, I believe you have.

442
00:35:01,632 --> 00:35:03,725
- We shouldn't have left him.
- We had no choice.

443
00:35:03,801 --> 00:35:06,702
What if Carter isn't one of us?
What if he tells the Sheriff?

444
00:35:06,771 --> 00:35:08,830
Then Robin's dead.

445
00:35:12,643 --> 00:35:14,634
I received your letter.

446
00:35:14,745 --> 00:35:16,610
I was about to come and visit you.

447
00:35:16,681 --> 00:35:19,844
I asked to be left alone
and still you were coming to see me?

448
00:35:20,618 --> 00:35:22,586
You knew I would.

449
00:35:22,653 --> 00:35:24,416
Yes.

450
00:35:25,156 --> 00:35:27,124
And that's why I came.

451
00:35:27,758 --> 00:35:31,159
To ask you to please leave me be.

452
00:35:31,229 --> 00:35:33,959
Marian,

453
00:35:36,367 --> 00:35:39,097
you seriously expect me to believe

454
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:41,897
that you have given yourself to God?

455
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:45,500
Trust me, I haven't
given myself to anybody.

456
00:35:46,677 --> 00:35:48,508
Not yet.

457
00:35:48,579 --> 00:35:51,047
Good. Because, until you do,

458
00:35:52,016 --> 00:35:55,508
I will always believe that
there is a chance for you and me.

459
00:35:55,586 --> 00:35:58,054
- I need to think.
- Stop thinking.

460
00:35:58,156 --> 00:35:59,646
Come home to me.

461
00:36:00,625 --> 00:36:02,991
You burned my home to the ground.

462
00:36:03,828 --> 00:36:05,591
Marian...

463
00:36:07,598 --> 00:36:09,862
if I could take that back,

464
00:36:09,967 --> 00:36:13,926
if I could show you the side to me that
wants to build a home, not burn it down.

465
00:36:14,005 --> 00:36:17,202
- I've seen it.
- Then why do you reject it?

466
00:36:17,875 --> 00:36:19,843
My father is dead.

467
00:36:21,812 --> 00:36:24,144
I need time to grieve.

468
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:30,120
What better way to grieve
than to create new life?

469
00:36:30,188 --> 00:36:31,951
Marian,

470
00:36:32,023 --> 00:36:34,548
I thought that I might never see you again.

471
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:38,019
I thought I might never...

472
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:40,793
What?

473
00:36:43,501 --> 00:36:45,264
Kiss you.

474
00:36:51,142 --> 00:36:54,202
Oh, sorry. Er, Sheriff wants you.

475
00:36:54,845 --> 00:36:57,109
He's gonna put Robin's head on a spike.

476
00:37:02,787 --> 00:37:05,255
We must continue this conversation soon.

477
00:37:05,856 --> 00:37:07,551
Guy!

478
00:37:13,965 --> 00:37:16,399
I might have more work for you.
You staying in England?

479
00:37:16,467 --> 00:37:18,162
I may return to the Holy Land.

480
00:37:18,236 --> 00:37:21,467
Oh. Not to help King Richard?

481
00:37:21,572 --> 00:37:23,631
I've had enough of fighting Saracens.

482
00:37:23,741 --> 00:37:27,040
I would, however,
like to learn more of their tricks.

483
00:37:27,144 --> 00:37:30,307
They're way ahead of us
with potions and remedies.

484
00:37:31,415 --> 00:37:35,112
They make a concoction to reduce
the breathing of a man to nothing.

485
00:37:36,287 --> 00:37:39,586
- He seems to be dead but is not.
- Fascinating.

486
00:37:39,657 --> 00:37:41,625
A clue.

487
00:37:41,692 --> 00:37:44,786
And when the same man
drinks the opposing concoction,

488
00:37:44,862 --> 00:37:47,023
he comes back to life.

489
00:37:47,598 --> 00:37:49,759
Just like that.

490
00:37:49,834 --> 00:37:52,928
- Really? Just like what?
- Just like this.

491
00:37:58,009 --> 00:37:59,738
Alive?

492
00:38:00,478 --> 00:38:02,105
Oh.

493
00:38:04,782 --> 00:38:06,977
Oh, really.

494
00:38:07,051 --> 00:38:10,214
- I'll take that money.
- I'm not paying you now.

495
00:38:10,288 --> 00:38:13,155
Now that the stiff
has stepped off the stretcher.

496
00:38:15,026 --> 00:38:17,187
- Kneel.
- Make me.

497
00:38:17,828 --> 00:38:20,194
- Ah!
- Pleasure.

498
00:38:26,704 --> 00:38:29,264
- What's she doing here?
- She saved your life.

499
00:38:31,876 --> 00:38:34,003
Guy,

500
00:38:34,078 --> 00:38:35,705
I have to go.

501
00:38:35,780 --> 00:38:39,147
- Go? You can't go.
- I can.

502
00:38:39,216 --> 00:38:42,117
And I must. Look, this was a mistake.

503
00:38:42,186 --> 00:38:45,314
No, this was the most perfect thing
that has ever happened.

504
00:38:45,389 --> 00:38:47,357
I'm grieving, Guy.

505
00:38:47,425 --> 00:38:49,518
I misled you. I'm sorry.

506
00:38:50,795 --> 00:38:54,322
- I'm sorry.
- You're misleading yourself.

507
00:38:54,398 --> 00:38:56,457
I know. I've done it.

508
00:38:56,567 --> 00:38:58,432
I told myself I didn't need you.

509
00:38:59,437 --> 00:39:01,428
That other things would satisfy me.

510
00:39:01,505 --> 00:39:03,666
Politics, power.

511
00:39:04,842 --> 00:39:08,403
- Yet here we are.
- I have to get back

512
00:39:08,479 --> 00:39:10,140
before they realize I'm missing.

513
00:39:10,214 --> 00:39:11,943
- Back to the convent?
- Yes.

514
00:39:12,016 --> 00:39:14,211
Marian, no.

515
00:39:15,052 --> 00:39:17,384
I forbid you to go.

516
00:39:24,195 --> 00:39:26,163
See you back at the camp.

517
00:39:32,636 --> 00:39:36,538
- Alarm, alarm!
- Well, looks like they're missing us.

518
00:39:36,607 --> 00:39:38,734
- They're in the castle!
- You ready?

519
00:39:38,809 --> 00:39:42,575
You sure you don't want to kill anyone?
We're more likely to get killed ourselves.

520
00:39:42,646 --> 00:39:45,137
Ah. Come on, we're much too good for that.

521
00:39:45,816 --> 00:39:48,114
- All right. Let's find out.
- Come on.

522
00:39:51,088 --> 00:39:53,113
Search everywhere!

523
00:40:08,239 --> 00:40:10,002
Carter! Quick.

524
00:40:14,812 --> 00:40:16,336
Ah!

525
00:40:52,082 --> 00:40:53,709
- Robin. Here!
- Robin!

526
00:40:58,656 --> 00:41:00,624
Ah!

527
00:41:02,393 --> 00:41:05,851
- Do you do this often?
- I seem to, yeah.

528
00:41:05,963 --> 00:41:09,364
- It really would be simpler to kill 'em.
- I know.

529
00:41:09,433 --> 00:41:11,401
But where would be the fun in that, eh?

530
00:41:15,840 --> 00:41:17,432
I'd better be off.

531
00:41:17,508 --> 00:41:19,976
- Are you sure you don't wanna stay?
- I do.

532
00:41:20,044 --> 00:41:25,141
But I'm going back to the Holy Land. I want to
visit my brother's grave, say goodbye properly.

533
00:41:25,216 --> 00:41:26,843
Tell him I'm sorry.

534
00:41:26,917 --> 00:41:28,782
Thought I was honoring his memory.

535
00:41:30,221 --> 00:41:33,713
And I thought I could do something useful,
warn King Richard for you.

536
00:41:35,793 --> 00:41:37,556
Thank you.

537
00:41:41,565 --> 00:41:43,726
Well,

538
00:41:43,801 --> 00:41:46,463
- you disobeyed me.
- I saved your life.

539
00:41:47,171 --> 00:41:49,162
And you kissed Gisborne.

540
00:41:49,240 --> 00:41:52,732
- And you tied me up.
- And you could have got us all killed.

541
00:41:52,810 --> 00:41:54,641
I'm sorry.

542
00:41:55,813 --> 00:41:58,281
I'm not used to taking orders.

543
00:41:58,382 --> 00:42:00,145
But I can learn.

544
00:42:01,285 --> 00:42:03,480
I'd like to be part of your gang.

545
00:42:04,522 --> 00:42:08,788
And I'm not used to you being
in the forest but... I'll learn.

546
00:42:10,427 --> 00:42:13,828
- Truce?
- Yeah. Truce.

547
00:42:16,867 --> 00:42:18,835
Safe journey, my friend.

